            <ArticleTitle>Torsion of intra-abdominal testicle. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>483-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 19-year-old youth with known right cryptorchidism had repeated attacks of acute abdominal symptoms, previously transient but now intensifying. Surgical exploration revealed a gangrenous intra-abdominal testis, which was successfully removed. Histologic examination confirmed the diagnosis of torsion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
